$-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x(x+11)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(-)\\cdot (+)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $x(x+11)>0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $x(x+11)$ is positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-11)$ and $(0,\\infty ).$ \nTherefore, we conclude that ${x}^{2}+11x>0$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-115864" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81cf9097a0d21d1b4f4cc54de9b422aed0ce63fb7c75b17e91228249c6fdc7ee"} {"question" "q-115864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-115864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-11,0)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (0,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (11,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,0)\\cup (11,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (0,11)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-115864" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (-\\infty ,-11)\\cup (0,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/