\n\nWe see that the expression is negative on the interval $(0,5).$ Also, we know that the expression equals $0$ at the points $x=0$ and $x=5.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $2{x}^{2}-10x\\le 0$ for all \n\n$$\nx\\in [0,5].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-277162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81cf9097a0d21d1b4f4cc54de9b422aed0ce63fb7c75b17e91228249c6fdc7ee"} {"question" "q-277162" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-277162" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-277162" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-277162" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e55766193495267