wing result:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $(x+5)(x-2)$ | $(-)\\cdot (-)=+$ | $(+)\\cdot (-)=-$ | $(+)\\cdot (+)=+$ |\n\nFinally, to solve the quadratic inequality $(x+5)(x-2)\\ge 0,$ we look at the bottom row to find out where the expression $(x+5)(x-2)$ is zero or positive.\n\nWe see that the expression is positive on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-5)$ and $(2,\\infty ).$ Also, we know that the expression equals $0$ at the points $x=-5$ and $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{2}+\\frac{3}{5}x\\ge 2$ for all $x\\in (-\\infty ,-5]\\cup [2,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-116200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "81cf9097a0d21d1b4f4cc54de9b422aed0ce63fb7c75b17e91228249c6fdc7ee"} {"question" "q-116200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c20850ad3771ad4731b37ee8d4fcfbb55b2151635"} {"question" "q-116200" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2]\\cup [5,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-5]\\cup [2,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,2]\\cup [5,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-2,5]"] ["math" "x\\in [-5,2]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13969014/state.json" "file_sha256" "555e557661934952678d0b5c